Comment (internal/service/relational/suggestions/prompt.go:63):
**Blocker — this schema is rejected by the Anthropic API at runtime; every cell fails.** Observed in production:

```
llm: output did not match schema: 400 Bad Request invalid_request_error
output_config.format.schema: For 'object' type, 'additionalProperties: object' is not supported. Please set 'additionalProperties' to false
```

Anthropic's strict structured-output mode requires every `object` to declare `additionalProperties: false`; it does not accept a *schema-valued* `additionalProperties` (an open-ended dynamic-key map). `sanitizeAnthropicSchema` in `internal/service/llm/anthropic.go` only strips numeric/length keywords, so this reaches the API and 400s — meaning the whole `proposed_filter_labels` feature this PR adds never produces a single suggestion.\n\nDynamic-key maps can't be expressed under strict mode. The standard fix is to model the labels as an **array of `{key, value}` objects**, each with `additionalProperties: false`, and fold that back into a map on decode:\n\n```go\n"proposed_filter_labels": map[string]any{\n    "type": "array",\n    "items": map[string]any{\n        "type":                 "object",\n        "additionalProperties": false,\n        "required":             []any{"key", "value"},\n        "properties": map[string]any{\n            "key":   map[string]any{"type": "string"},\n            "value": map[string]any{"type": "string"},\n        },\n    },\n},\n```\n\nThen change `RawMapping.ProposedFilterLabels` (validation.go:60) to decode the pair array into `map[string]string` (e.g. a named type with a custom `UnmarshalJSON`, so existing map-based tests/`validateProposedFilterLabels` are unaffected). Worth a unit test that decodes the array wire form and one asserting the schema stays a strict array, since none of the current tests exercise the real LLM JSON shape.
Implementation guidance: Fix the Anthropic structured-output schema for proposed_filter_labels while preserving the internal map-based validation semantics. In internal/service/relational/suggestions/prompt.go, change OutputSchema so proposed_filter_labels is an array, not an object map: type array, items type object, additionalProperties false, required ["key", "value"], properties key/value both strings. Keep proposed_filter_labels required at the mapping level. Update the system prompt wording if needed so the model understands proposed_filter_labels is a list of key/value pairs, not a JSON object. In internal/service/relational/suggestions/validation.go, replace RawMapping.ProposedFilterLabels map[string]string with a small named type that stores/behaves as map[string]string for validateProposedFilterLabels, but implements UnmarshalJSON to accept the new wire form [{"key":"...","value":"..."}]. To avoid breaking existing tests and any non-Anthropic callers, the custom unmarshal should also accept the legacy object form {"provider":"aws"} and normalize both forms into the same map. For the array form, trim or reject empty keys consistently with existing validation behavior; if duplicate keys appear, let the last decoded value win or explicitly reject, but document the chosen behavior in a focused test. Do not change validateProposedFilterLabels' existing sanitation rules: continue dropping _agent/_plugin, requiring remaining key/value pairs to match the evidence labels, injecting _policy from evidence when present, and using the constrained fallback only when appropriate. Add tests covering: OutputSchema uses an array item object for proposed_filter_labels and every object in that schema path has additionalProperties false; ValidateMappings/RawMapping JSON decoding accepts the new pair-array wire form and produces the same validated ProposedFilterLabelSet as the old map form; and existing legacy map-form tests still pass.
